WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.880
What happens to a person when proprioceptive input is lost?

2
00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:11.773
Picture reaching for a cup in a lit room, with your stretch lines silent.

3
00:00:12.783 --> 00:00:17.003
Predict. What would you have to rely on to know where your arm is?

4
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:26.447
Mainly your eyes. Vision does much of the work.

5
00:00:27.247 --> 00:00:30.007
Take it away too, and reaching becomes far less accurate.

6
00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:37.967
Chesler and colleagues reported two unrelated young people with inactivating

7
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:40.307
variants in both copies of PIEZO2.

8
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:43.557
Reaching was tested with and without sight.

9
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:49.317
Without vision, their uncoordinated movements and misjudged reaches became markedly

10
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:50.317
worse.

11
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.810
Yet they could still walk, talk and write, though one walked only with support.

12
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.073
An older case shows the daily cost.

13
00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:00.333
A man known as I.W.

14
00:01:00.473 --> 00:01:03.053
had lost large-fibre sensation below the neck.

15
00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:06.257
He lacked light touch and position sense.

16
00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:10.117
But he kept pain, temperature and the sense of muscle fatigue.

17
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:14.597
In testing, he could make no new movement without watching it.

18
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:16.857
Every new movement had to be watched.

19
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.090
Both cases show the rule's second half.

20
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.070
With proprioceptive input lost, accurate movement depends heavily on vision.

21
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.650
Neither case silences spindles alone; touch was affected too.

22
00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:33.893
In mice, the line turned out to matter for the skeleton too.

23
00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:40.707
Deleting Piezo2 with a parvalbumin driver curved the spine in some mice by postnatal

24
00:01:40.707 --> 00:01:41.707
day 60.

25
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:47.467
Deleting it in bone and cartilage lineages did not curve the spine, at the ages

26
00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:48.467
tested.

27
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:51.197
The authors read this as non-autonomous.

28
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:56.717
The curve shows in the skeleton, but the gene was lost in parvalbumin-labelled

29
00:01:56.717 --> 00:01:57.717
neurons.

30
00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.720
How the signal reaches the skeleton is not known.

31
00:02:01.683 --> 00:02:03.063
One limit to remember.

32
00:02:03.063 --> 00:02:08.083
Near a joint's limits, and for the feeling of effort, the stretch rule is not the

33
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.083
whole story.

34
00:02:09.683 --> 00:02:13.583
So limb position is an estimate built mainly from the stretch line.

35
00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:17.123
Lose that input, and vision does much of its work.
